{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_dnsseedprovider", "label": "DnsSeedProvider", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Loest Seeds beim Start via DNS auf. Cluster.join blockiert auf der Aufloesung, langsames DNS ist also reale Boot-Verzoegerung; ein leeres Ergebnis laesst den lokalen Node sich selbst bootstrappen, was nur beim ersten Node gewollt ist."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_dnsseedprovideroptionstype", "label": "DnsSeedProviderOptionsType", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "hostname, systemName, port, useSrv, cacheTtlMs, pinnedAddresses, log sowie ueberschreibbare resolve/resolveSrv-Funktionen - letztere vor allem, damit Tests ohne echten Resolver laufen."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_srv_record_mode", "label": "SRV-Record-Modus", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Empfohlen, weil SRV-Records Host, Port, Weight und Priority pro Eintrag tragen und DNS-SD-Tools (Consul, Eureka) sie automatisch publizieren. SRV loest zu Ziel-Hostnames auf, gepinnt wird deshalb mit Host-Suffixen."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_a_record_mode", "label": "A-Record-Modus", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fuer Setups ohne SRV: DNS traegt nur IPs, der Provider paart jede mit dem konfigurierten Port. Gepinnt wird hier mit CIDRs, weil A-Records zu IP-Adressen aufloesen."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_pinnedaddresses", "label": "pinnedAddresses (DNS)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "DNS-Antworten kommen von einer Gegenstelle, die der Node nie authentifiziert hat; die Pin-Liste begrenzt, was diese Antwort sagen darf. Eine Liste, die im konfigurierten Modus nichts treffen kann, wird bei der Konstruktion abgelehnt statt still jeden Record zu verwerfen - sonst saehe eine zu enge Liste von aussen aus wie eine leere DNS-Antwort. Verworfene Adressen sind gefiltert, nicht fatal, und gehen an log."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_canonical_address_form", "label": "Kanonische Adressform beim Pin-Vergleich", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nicht-kanonische Schreibweisen (1e1.0.0.1, 010.0.0.1, 0x0a.0.0.1) lesen sich fuer einen grosszuegigen Parser als 10.0.0.1, aber die Socket-Schicht wertet sie als keine IP und loest sie ueber DNS auf - eine solche Antwort kaeme an einem 10.0.0.0/8-Pin vorbei. Alles Nicht-Kanonische gilt darum als Hostname und wird nie gegen einen CIDR-Pin geprueft; ein Tippfehler wie 10.0.0.0/ wirft, statt wie frueher als /0 den gesamten Adressraum zuzulassen."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_dns_ttl_cache", "label": "In-Process-TTL-Cache (cacheTtlMs)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "lookup() ist kein Einmal-Aufruf - Bootstrap und uebergeordnete Retry-Logik rufen es erneut. Der Cache (Default 60000 ms, 0 deaktiviert) haelt wiederholte Aufrufe von DNS fern; fehlgeschlagene Lookups werden bewusst nicht gecacht."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_pinning_is_defense_in_depth", "label": "Pinning als Defense-in-Depth, nicht als primaere Kontrolle", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wer joinen darf, entscheidet mTLS: das Zertifikat eines Peers muss fuer die beanspruchte Adresse buergen. Pinning zaehlt dort, wo mTLS nicht konfiguriert ist, und als zweite Schicht dort, wo es das ist. Im SRV-Modus ist ein Suffix-Pin schwaecher, weil der A-Lookup des Ziels selbst nicht gepinnt ist."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_dnsseedprovider", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_dnsseedprovideroptionstype", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_dnsseedprovider", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_srv_record_mode", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_dnsseedprovider", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_a_record_mode", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_dnsseedprovider", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_pinnedaddresses", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_dnsseedprovider", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_dns_ttl_cache", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_canonical_address_form", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_pinnedaddresses", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_pinning_is_defense_in_depth", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_pinnedaddresses", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_pinnedaddresses", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_srv_record_mode", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_pinnedaddresses", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_a_record_mode", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_dnsseedprovider", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_kubernetes_api_kubernetesapiseedprovider", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_dnsseedprovider", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_config_configseedprovider", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_dns_dnsseedprovider", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_discovery_seed_providers_aggregate_aggregateseedprovider", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/discovery/seed-providers/dns.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}], "hyperedges": []}